WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 9.1 · Financial Management
Finance roles and the finance cycle

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Decide who does, records and oversees your money before the first payment.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
Financial management is how you plan, record, check and report your money. It has three layers, and it works best when you decide who does each part before money starts to move.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
Three layers of finance

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:38.611
Bookkeeping: Recording every transaction accurately, from the very first payment you make. For example: Our bakery logs each flour order and each day’s stall takings, with a receipt.

6
00:00:38.611 --> 00:00:50.311
Accounting: Turning those records into reports that follow rules, such as annual accounts and tax returns. For example: Once registered, an accountant prepares the bakery’s annual accounts from its records.

7
00:00:50.311 --> 00:01:02.470
Management finance: Using the numbers to plan and decide: budgets, forecasts, pricing and cost control. For example: The founders check what each loaf costs before setting the stall’s prices.

8
00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:03.470
Why roles come first

9
00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:09.515
1. Separating doing, recording and overseeing is a control, even for two people.

10
00:01:09.515 --> 00:01:15.930
2. Habits set before the first payment are far easier than fixing them later.

11
00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:22.974
3. An accountant early shows how your legal form affects tax and accounts.

12
00:01:23.374 --> 00:01:23.974
What it shapes

13
00:01:23.974 --> 00:01:28.907
1. Your finance cycle: plan, record, control, report and review.

14
00:01:28.907 --> 00:01:34.581
2. Your calendar from Module 5: year end, accounts and tax dates.

15
00:01:34.581 --> 00:01:40.885
3. Every lesson in this module: budgets, cash, controls and reports.

16
00:01:41.285 --> 00:01:41.885
What to avoid

17
00:01:41.885 --> 00:01:47.559
One person doing, recording and checking everything, with nobody else looking.

18
00:01:47.559 --> 00:01:52.493
Waiting until after registration to talk to an accountant.

19
00:01:52.493 --> 00:01:58.056
Assuming rules from another country apply to you.

20
00:01:58.656 --> 00:02:00.456
You write your finance roles and your monthly and annual cycle.

21
00:02:00.456 --> 00:02:04.456
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:05.956 --> 00:02:09.056
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
